---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy — Notare"
  description="How Notare handles your data — local-first, nothing uploaded to us."
>
  <section class="band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="kicker">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="section-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="section-lede">
        Notare stores your meeting data locally. Connections you enable can
        send data to your chosen speech, AI, calendar, email, or paired devices.
      </p>

      <div class="prose">
        <p class="updated">Last updated: 14 November 2026</p>

        <h2 id="overview">1. Overview</h2>
        <p>
          Notare is a free, open-source (MIT-licensed), local-first meeting
          notetaker and dictation app. This policy covers the desktop app and
          notare.dev. You do not need a Notare account. You choose whether to
          connect external services; those services have their own privacy policies.
        </p>

        <h2 id="no-accounts">2. No accounts, no telemetry</h2>
        <p>
          Notare requires no Notare sign-up. The app ships with analytics and
          telemetry compiled out. This does not mean the app makes no network
          requests: updates, model downloads, and connected services need network access.
        </p>

        <h2 id="local-storage">3. Your content is stored locally</h2>
        <p>
          Notare stores its database, app settings, and recordings on your
          computer. You can save notes as Markdown in a folder you choose.
          You control these files and their backups. Optional device sync
          shares supported meeting data with the devices you pair.
        </p>

        <h2 id="transcription">4. Transcription</h2>
        <p>
          You can download a speech model and transcribe on your device.
          If you configure a remote speech provider or a self-hosted companion
          server, Notare sends audio to that endpoint for transcription.
          Review that service's privacy policy and your server configuration
          before sending recordings.
        </p>

        <h2 id="google-calendar">5. Google Calendar (optional connection)</h2>
        <p>
          Connecting Google Calendar is entirely optional. If you choose to
          connect it:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            Notare uses Google's OAuth through a local loopback flow on your own
            machine (<code>127.0.0.1</code>).
          </li>
          <li>
            The initial connection requests <strong>read-only</strong> calendar
            access (<code>calendar.readonly</code> and
            <code>calendar.events.readonly</code>) plus your email address
            (<code>userinfo.email</code>) to identify the connected account.
            If you create a calendar event, Notare requests the additional
            <code>calendar.events</code> write permission.
          </li>
          <li>
            The resulting OAuth tokens are stored
            <strong>locally, in your operating system's keychain or credential
            store</strong>, on your device.
          </li>
          <li>
            Calendar data supports upcoming-meeting views, attached notes,
            and meeting preparation.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          The OAuth exchange happens between your device and Google, not
          through the Notare website. You can disconnect a Google account
          in Settings to remove its stored credentials.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Gmail is a separate, optional connection.</strong>
          It requests <code>gmail.compose</code> to create follow-up drafts
          in your Gmail account. That permission includes composing and sending
          mail; Notare's follow-up workflow creates a draft for you to review
          and send yourself. Draft generation uses your configured AI backend.
        </p>
        <p>
          Outlook is also optional. Initial access uses
          <code>offline_access</code>, <code>User.Read</code>, and
          <code>Calendars.Read</code>. Creating an event requests
          <code>Calendars.ReadWrite</code>. Your device communicates with Microsoft.
        </p>
        <p class="disclosure">
          Notare's use and transfer of information received from Google APIs to
          any other app will adhere to the
          <a
            href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy"
            >Google API Services User Data Policy</a
          >, including the Limited Use requirements.
        </p>

        <h2 id="ai-enhancement">6. Optional AI enhancement</h2>
        <p>
          AI enhancement, briefs, draft generation, and chat use the backend
          you configure. A remote backend receives the notes, transcripts,
          questions, and other context needed for the requested feature.
          Local backends such as Ollama can keep that processing on your
          computer. The provider's policies govern any data you send to it.
        </p>
        <h3>Optional device sync (preview)</h3>
        <p>
          Sync is off by default. If you enable it and pair devices, Notare
          sends supported notes and meeting data to those peers. The iroh
          transport uses public discovery and relay services operated by
          Number 0 (n0.computer); relayed sync content is end-to-end encrypted.
          You can stop sync or remove paired devices in Settings.
        </p>
        <h3>Optional MCP access</h3>
        <p>
          If you enable the MCP server and connect an agent client, that
          client can use the meeting tools you expose. The client's own AI
          backend may receive the returned data. Review its configuration.
        </p>

        <h2 id="website">7. The notare.dev website</h2>
        <p>
          Cloudflare serves this static website and may process request
          information such as your IP address and requested URL for delivery,
          security, and reliability. Cloudflare also injects its Web Analytics
          script into the live website for page-view and performance
          measurements. This is separate from the desktop app, which has no telemetry.
          See <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare's privacy policy</a>.
          Product screenshots use fictional demo data. Download and source
          links take you to GitHub, which has its own privacy policy.
        </p>

        <h2 id="retention">8. Data retention &amp; deletion</h2>
        <p>
          You manage your local files and backups. The app also offers
          audio-retention settings. Removing a local copy does not delete
          copies you exported, sent to an external service, or backed up.
          Disconnecting a calendar or email account removes its stored
          credentials from this device.
        </p>

        <h2 id="children">9. Children</h2>
        <p>Notare is not directed at children under 13.</p>

        <h2 id="changes">10. Changes</h2>
        <p>
          This policy may be updated from time to time. The "Last updated" date
          above always reflects the latest version.
        </p>

        <h2 id="contact">11. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about this policy or Notare's data practices can be raised
          via the project's
          <a href="https://github.com/abhi-wan-kenobi/notare"
            >GitHub repository</a
          >, or through the developer contact listed on the OAuth consent
          screen.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .prose {
    max-width: 70ch;
    margin-top: 40px;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }
  .prose .updated {
    font-family: "JetBrains Mono", ui-monospace, "SF Mono", Menlo, Consolas,
      monospace;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    padding-bottom: 24px;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .prose h2 {
    font-size: 20px;
    font-weight: 640;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-top: 40px;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
    line-height: 1.3;
    scroll-margin-top: 80px;
  }
  .prose h3 {
    font-size: 16.5px;
    font-weight: 620;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-top: 28px;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }
  .prose p {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }
  .prose strong {
    color: var(--text);
    font-weight: 620;
  }
  .prose ul {
    margin: 0 0 16px;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    display: grid;
    gap: 10px;
  }
  .prose li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 22px;
  }
  .prose li::before {
    content: "—";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  .prose a {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
    text-decoration-color: var(--accent);
  }
  .prose a:hover {
    text-decoration-color: var(--accent);
  }
  .prose code {
    font-family: "JetBrains Mono", ui-monospace, "SF Mono", Menlo, Consolas,
      monospace;
    font-size: 0.86em;
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 4px;
    padding: 1px 6px;
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .prose .disclosure {
    margin-top: 24px;
    padding: 18px 20px;
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--accent);
    border-radius: var(--radius-panel);
    font-size: 15px;
    color: var(--text);
  }
</style>
